<div class="prose prose-ncs-dark bg-ncs-dark-700 p-4 rounded shadow max-w-none">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

  <p>Last updated: <time>1 May, 2026</time></p>

  <h2 id="section-1" class="mt-2">1. Data Sharing</h2>
  <h3 id="section-1-1">1.1 Selling of data</h3>
  <p>
    NeedCoolerShoes does not, and will never, sell any information whatsoever to third parties.
  </p>

  <h3 id="section-1-2">1.2 Sharing data with third parties</h3>
  <p>
    NeedCoolerShoes will only share data with third parties if we rely on them for a service, and if so, only data that is required for them to provide said service. Information about what data is shared, and what third party services are used, can be found in <a href="#section-3">Section 3</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    The only other case where we will share information with a third party is if we are legally required to by law. If NeedCoolerShoes is legally forced to share information / data, we will share only the bare minimum required to comply with the law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="section-2">2. Data Collection</h2>
  <p>
    The following data might be collected and stored by NeedCoolerShoes, as part of normal site operation.

    <ul>
      <li>IPv4 / IPv6 address(es)</li>
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>Username</li>
      <li>Display name</li>
      <li>Date of last login</li>
      <li>Amount of times the user logged in</li>
      <li>Username and UUID of any connected Minecraft accounts</li>
      <li>Actions performed by moderators</li>
      <li>Any content uploaded to the site</li>
      <li>Application log files and error reports that may contain user information</li>
    </ul>

    Users may at any time request a copy of all data related to them stored in our database. Such requests can be sent to dev (at) needcoolershoes.com, and must be sent from the email address connected to the user account in question, or otherwise adequate proof of ownership must be provided.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Users may also request their account be deleted, to the same email, granted they have adequate proof of ownership of said account.
    Copies of account data might still persist in site data backups however. If this is an issue, we can remove it from backups,
    but this is a much lengthier process and we would rather not have to do so.
  </p>

  <h2 id="section-3">3. Third Party Services</h2>
  <h3 id="section-3-1">3.1 Counter</h3>
  <p>
    NeedCoolerShoes collects anonymous analytics data using Counter. For transparency, the analytics for the site is public,
    and can be viewed at <a href="https://counter.dev/dashboard.html?user=Moxvallix&token=d7TgWkme7Jo%3D">counter.dev</a>.
    
    Quoting from Counter's privacy policy, the following information is collected:
    <blockquote>
      Your personalized tracking script aggregates the following statistical information of your users.

      <ul>
        <li>The day of the week (As in: Monday, Tuesday, ...)</li>
        <li>Your users device (As in Phone, Tablet or Computer)</li>
        <li>The date of the visit</li>
        <li>From which other website a visit originated.</li>
        <li>The users browser (As in: Firefox, Chrome, Microsoft Edge, ...)</li>
        <li>The hour component of the current time in a day</li>
        <li>A country mapped to the users IP address.</li>
        <li>The users operating system (As in: Windows or Mac)</li>
        <li>Information on the users screen size</li>
        <li>The users preferred language</li>
        <li>Pages visited</li>
      </ul>

      These data points are saved anonymously in our primary database aggregated on a hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, yearly and overall basis. Counter deletes hourly, daily, weekly and monthly statistics after a certain time period. You can e.g. access data from this month, but not data from last month. We try to improve your users privacy by "forgetting" their data as time passes. We do not keep single data points on your users but only statistical, that is aggregated data.
    </blockquote>

    Counter was chosen for site analytics for its focus on privacy, and the fact that it was open source.
    <a href="https://counter.dev/pages/privacy.html">Link to Counter's privacy policy.</a>
  </p>

  <h3 id="section-3-2">3.2 SMTP2GO</h3>
  <p>
    NeedCoolerShoes uses SMTP2GO for transactional emails, such as when a user resets their password. As they are an emailing service, data such as email addresses, as well as the contents of the email, is submitted to them, such that they can send the email. NeedCoolerShoes will only share data required
    to send the given email, and will only send emails using SMTP2GO in response to a user's request, such as a reset password request, or potentially for
    email validation at sign up. <a href="https://www.smtp2go.com/privacy/">Link to SMTP2GO's privacy policy.</a>
  </p>

  <h3 id="section-3-3">3.3 Cloudflare</h3>
  <p>
    NeedCoolerShoes is served through Cloudflare's proxy for DDOS and scraping protection. Due to the nature of Cloudflare's proxy, it being able to decrypt
    all site traffic being core to its functionality, limits what data we can theoretically restrict Cloudflare from collecting. As such, it would be a good idea
    to read through their privacy policy if it is of concern. <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Link to Cloudflare's privacy policy.</a>
  </p>

  <h3 id="section-3-4">3.4 Crunchbits</h3>
  <p>NeedCoolerShoes is hosted on Crunchbits. <a href="https://crunchbits.com/legal/privacy">Link to Crunchbits' privacy policy.</a></p>

  <h3 id="section-3-5">3.5 HostHatch</h3>
  <p>NeedCoolerShoes stores log data and backups on HostHatch. <a href="https://hosthatch.com/privacy-policy">Link to HostHatch's privacy policy.</a></p>

  <h3 id="section-3-6">3.6 Discord</h3>
  <p>
    NeedCoolerShoes logs some data to Discord, for moderators to review. This includes messages sent through the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>,
    new user registrations, and newly uploaded skins. <a href="https://discord.com/privacy">Link to Discord's privacy policy.</a>
  </p>

  <h4 id="section-3-6-1">3.6.1 Messages</h4>
  <p>
    The following data is logged to private channels on Discord when a site message is sent:

    <ul>
      <li>Provided name</li>
      <li>Provided contact method / email address</li>
      <li>Message title</li>
      <li>Message body</li>
      <li>Answer to the captcha</li>
      <li>Anything written to the hidden honeypot field</li>
      <li>IPv4 / IPv6 address(es)</li>
      <li>User Agent</li>
    </ul>

    The last two items are collected to analyse spam requests that are sent through the form on a frequent basis.
  </p>

  <h4 id="section-3-6-2">3.6.2 New user registrations</h4>
  <p>
    The following data is logged to private channels on Discord when a user signs up:

    <ul>
      <li>Username</li>
      <li>Email (with name part redacted)</li>
      <li>Answer to the captcha</li>
      <li>Anything written to the hidden honeypot field</li>
      <li>IPv4 / IPv6 address(es)</li>
      <li>User Agent</li>
    </ul>

    This information is logged to monitor and moderate spam accounts.
  </p>

  <h4 id="section-3-6-3">3.6.3 New skins</h4>
  <p>
    The following data is logged to a public channel on Discord when a public skin is shared to the gallery:

    <ul>
      <li>Skin title</li>
      <li>Username</li>
      <li>Skin URL</li>
      <li>Skin description</li>
      <li>2D preview of the skin</li>
    </ul>

    This information is logged to a public channel to allow all members of the Discord to see when a new skin is posted.
  </p>

  <h3 id="section-3-7">3.7 Cloudinary</h3>
  <p>NeedCoolerShoes hosts some images on Cloudinary. <a href="https://cloudinary.com/privacy">Link to Cloudinary's privacy policy.</a></p>

  <h2 id="section-4">4. Cookies and Site Data</h2>
  <p>
    NeedCoolerShoes uses cookies to keep users signed in to the site across page refreshes. NeedCoolerShoes also utilises local browser storage for remembering projects in the various editors. NeedCoolerShoes does not utilise either of these types of data storage for any form of fingerprinting.

    However, <a href="#section-3-3">Cloudflare</a> also set their own cookies, so please refer to their privacy policy as well.
  </p>
</div>
